{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem","id":445481,"title":"Can a Werewolf Pack take a Strix or a Godmachine Angel as a totem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T01:52:05-07:00","id":445481,"title":"Can a Werewolf Pack take a Strix or a Godmachine Angel as a totem?","content":"What it says on the tin. A quick glance at the 2nd edition rules doesn't seem to preclude it, but I can't help but wonder if I'm missing something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:49:44-07:00","id":445560,"title":"","content":"Giving that the Totem has to be a Spirit (as in from the Hisil) and neither of those things qualify as such, I would say a clear No is in order. That said, the idea of a pack of werewolves in Tokyo with a Tengu (maybe a Strix?) as a Totem is too amusing to be deterred by such a minor thing.<br /> <br /> Note that they maybe part of the Pack, though (at least the Strix/Tengu, not so sure about the Angels) but not the Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:23:28-07:00","id":445574,"title":"","content":"Lycoan-Ur in Poland has some serious GM going on though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:28:07-07:00","id":445638,"title":"","content":"He might just be a key part of a large Infrastructure that relies on him and his lodge to generate Essence for the God-Machine. Which doesn't exclude him from being &quot;just&quot; a very powerful high primal urge Werewolf with a couple of nasty bans related to his ever present hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-17-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:40:26-07:00","id":445649,"title":"","content":"I'd &quot;allow it&quot; - but as a serious blasphemy that's going to have in-game social and metaphysical consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:33:27-07:00","id":445963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=445649#post445649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd &quot;allow it&quot; - but as a serious blasphemy that's going to have in-game social and metaphysical consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blasphemous Ghost Wolves is one of my favorite things anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:21:53-07:00","id":446441,"title":"","content":"A strix is not a spirit. It is not made of ephemera, nor does it use spirit mechanics. The rules for creating a totem wouldn't work. A strix can not become a totem any more than a vampire could.<br /> <br /> An angel is close enough to a spirit, but it lacks the ability to agree to the terms. If an angel agreed to be a totem then it would fall, turn into a demon. The God Machine would have to enter into the pact for an angel, essentially. This would make the pack agents of the GM. I think you want an Exile instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:35:19-07:00","id":446486,"title":"","content":"An Angel can be designed to serve as a Totem, which should make a pact ask what their higher purpose is if they aren't busy getting wrapped up in having a purpose.<br /> <br /> As for the Strix...Well, I don't discourage you from bending reality to allow deliciously terrible bad ideas to happen.<br /> <br /> Frequency, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:05:09-07:00","id":446821,"title":"","content":"Not usually, but I&quot;m sure angels can be created by the God-Machine who can. While it is unlikely, it wouldn't surprise me if a strix developed a really weird Dread Power that allowed them to become a Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:55:55-07:00","id":446876,"title":"","content":"A totem provides direction and identity to a pack. It isn't a matter of whether or not the God Machine can order an angel to become a totem. The point is you have a pack taking orders from the God Machine now. With an Exile, at least you wouldn't have werewolves doing the bidding of the God Machine.<br /> <br /> You could create a Dread Power that provides whatever bonuses you wanted a totem to give, but the strix would still not be a totem. Strix don't have bans therefore the pack can't take up their &quot;totem's&quot; ban. It just won't work and the better question is why bother?<br /> <br /> You could literally create a spirit that looks like a strix, acts like a strix and has abilities similar to a strix (it is the same for an angel for that matter), so why make things harder on yourself by forcing something that wasn't meant to be a totem to try to take the place of a totem? Make life easy and just create a spirit by taking what you like from an angel, a strix, a ghost, or whatever. Maybe the spirit ate one of those others to take up some of the same traits and abilities. It is easier to start with a spirit than force something that is not a spirit into a cookie cutter for a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:57:08-07:00","id":446879,"title":"","content":"As appears to be the general consensus, my view on this is &quot;No by default, but it'd be a damned cool plot hook to make an exception&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:30:03-07:00","id":446990,"title":"","content":"I could see a really cool plot being based off a pack with an angelic totem. Local packs have started to notice their very odd rites and can't figure out what the pack is trying to accomplish. Weird shit is certainly happening, but it doesn't seem to be tied to the Shadow. Perhaps they stumble on a stigmatic who can actually <i>see </i>what they are doing and induct her into their pack...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:44:32-07:00","id":447124,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with a NPC pack getting more or less taken over by an angel (strix or whatever) that is for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T22:04:53-07:00","id":447137,"title":"","content":"An Angel for a totem would probably be facilitated if it was one that operated primarily in the Shadow. Hi psychopomp. The Shadow has the advantage of not having &quot;frequencies&quot; like Twilight does, too. You're either there, or you're not.<br /> <br /> And well, Strix as pack members actually seems more plausible than one becoming a totem, and not all that strange in a territory like Japan. Mutual interests and all. Tengu seem much milder then Strix elsewhere. Or at least more polite.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it's possible for a Werewolf to get the Gift Of Death out of one in Twilight or in the Shadow. Or other, stranger Gifts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T22:15:37-07:00","id":447141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=447137#post447137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Angel for a totem would probably be facilitated if it was one that operated primarily in the Shadow. Hi psychopomp. The Shadow has the advantage of not having &quot;frequencies&quot; like Twilight does, too. You're either there, or you're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple things worth pointing out:<br /> <br /> 1. Most Wheel-work dealing with other dimensions amounts to dumping stuff through an Iris.<br /> 2. It's entirely plausible for the Machine to devise an angel that occupies the Shadow-ephemera band of Twilight by nature or Numen.<br /> 3. As much as I love the Wheels, I feel it's worth paying attention to the viability of other Incarnations for ephemeral infiltration; Destroyers are of a kind with hunter-angels, after all, and the Shields are overwhelmingly built for adaptability, to say nothing of the all-but-textually-established Messenger work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T00:38:51-07:00","id":447277,"title":"","content":"In one of the werewolf books, there's a pack that thinks their pack totem is a ghost. they're tragically tragically wrong, but the fact that the first response of all the local werewolves isn't &quot;Nope, not possible&quot; suggests to me that while extremely rare, such things might happen occasionally. <br /> <br /> Besides, the distinctions can be fluid. Bale hounds serve demons, so is as demon totem really that inconceivable? A demon could have originated as a spirit, goetia, or ghost.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, through consumption, can become part of a ghost-spirit magath, ditto ghosts stuck in the shadow can gain spiritual traits.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'd go with a no for Strix, while technically ephemerals, they barely qualify, they aren't even creatures of essence.<br /> <br /> So angels are a maybe. King lycaen, who is either an angel pretending to a werewolf or a werewolf/spirit/angel ninja/pirate/zombie, does serve as a lodge totem with aspirations towards tribal totem. If the god-machine can make an angel or an angel hybrid capable of serving as a lodge totem, I see no reason it can't make one that can serve as a pack totem (that being an inferior position after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T02:44:16-07:00","id":447437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=447277#post447277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the distinctions can be fluid. Bale hounds serve demons, so is as demon totem really that inconceivable? A demon could have originated as a spirit, goetia, or ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'd let Bale Hounds have straight up Dominions as Totems - the Malejin themselves are just the Archdemons (&quot;Wounds&quot; are openings between the Hisil &amp; the &quot;Hell&quot; of WoD: Inferno). Them not being native to the Hisil is why there isn't a proper First Tongue word for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:20:58-07:00","id":447587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=447141#post447141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple things worth pointing out:<br /> <br /> 1. Most Wheel-work dealing with other dimensions amounts to dumping stuff through an Iris.<br /> 2. It's entirely plausible for the Machine to devise an angel that occupies the Shadow-ephemera band of Twilight by nature or Numen.<br /> 3. As much as I love the Wheels, I feel it's worth paying attention to the viability of other Incarnations for ephemeral infiltration; Destroyers are of a kind with hunter-angels, after all, and the Shields are overwhelmingly built for adaptability, to say nothing of the all-but-textually-established Messenger work.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, Psychopomp just seemed like the most immediate logical role to find there, hence my little note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:26:11-07:00","id":447918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=447277#post447277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In one of the werewolf books, there's a pack that thinks their pack totem is a ghost. they're tragically tragically wrong, but the fact that the first response of all the local werewolves isn't &quot;Nope, not possible&quot; suggests to me that while extremely rare, such things might happen occasionally.<br /> <br /> Besides, the distinctions can be fluid. Bale hounds serve demons, so is as demon totem really that inconceivable? A demon could have originated as a spirit, goetia, or ghost.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, through consumption, can become part of a ghost-spirit magath, ditto ghosts stuck in the shadow can gain spiritual traits.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'd go with a no for Strix, while technically ephemerals, they barely qualify, they aren't even creatures of essence.<br /> <br /> So angels are a maybe. King lycaen, who is either an angel pretending to a werewolf or a werewolf/spirit/angel ninja/pirate/zombie, does serve as a lodge totem with aspirations towards tribal totem. If the god-machine can make an angel or an angel hybrid capable of serving as a lodge totem, I see no reason it can't make one that can serve as a pack totem (that being an inferior position after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pickering Family in the Rockies also don't have a normal spirit as a totem. They have something they summoned up from the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Mind, this is very early in 1e, before a lot of stuff was decided, it seems, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:32:02-07:00","id":447930,"title":"","content":"There's a few other totems that are implied to be strange and possibly not just spirits throughout the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:20:01-07:00","id":448152,"title":"","content":"Totally. Sounds like a great story hook for an NPC pack. I would not recommend letting a PC pack do it unless you want to run a thematically different kind of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:41:17-07:00","id":463124,"title":"","content":"So, fun crossover time-could a Pack take on a Geist as a totem normally?<br /> What if that Geist then Bargained with a Mortal and then became a Sin-Eater?<br /> Could a Pack benefit from a Krewe channel too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:52:34-07:00","id":463133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445481-can-a-werewolf-pack-take-a-strix-or-a-godmachine-angel-as-a-totem?p=463124#post463124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, fun crossover time-could a Pack take on a Geist as a totem normally?<br /> What if that Geist then Bargained with a Mortal and then became a Sin-Eater?<br /> Could a Pack benefit from a Krewe channel too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if Sin-eaters could benefit from pack bonuses it could work both ways..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T21:54:51-07:00","id":463137,"title":"","content":"Toss in a Changeling for a motley pact, and happy times abound!<br /> <br /> *Cackles* Even the first question alone has such fun possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}